#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/TcpClient.java:16
msgid ""
"Hello, world! Alice the buggle here: I painted the whole floor blue today."
msgstr ""

#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/TcpClient.java:17
msgid ""
"Sunny over the pond of the turtles: 25 degrees, a perfect day to draw "
"spirals."
msgstr ""

#. Translator: please keep this string unchanged (without the quotes): "%s"
#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/TcpClient.java:22
#, java-printf-format
msgid ""
"Dave was here, and he painted %s on the wall. Never trust what comes from "
"the network!"
msgstr ""

#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/TcpClient.java:23
msgid "Sorry for the delay: my turtle was finishing its spiral."
msgstr ""

#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/TcpClient.java:25
msgid ""
"Psst, newcomer! Bob here. I know where a real treasure is hidden, but the "
"walls have ears. Come and see me on the IRC server of BuggleInc, and I will "
"tell you more."
msgstr ""

#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/TcpFramingIrc.java:20
msgid "please"
msgstr ""

#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/TcpFramingIrc.java:20
#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/XmppClient.java:76
msgid "treasure"
msgstr ""

#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/TcpFramingIrc.java:23
msgid "Welcome, little buggles!"
msgstr ""

#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/TcpFramingIrc.java:24
msgid "Has anyone seen my brush? I left it near the wall."
msgstr ""

#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/TcpFramingIrc.java:25
#, java-format
msgid ""
"{0}: are you looking for something? Talk to me with \"PRIVMSG #welcome :Bob: "
"your message\"."
msgstr ""

#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/TcpFramingIrc.java:26
msgid "I painted the whole floor blue today, it looks like the sea!"
msgstr ""

#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/TcpFramingIrc.java:27
msgid "Turning left three times is the same as turning right, I swear."
msgstr ""

#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/TcpFramingIrc.java:28
msgid "Found it! It was under a baggle."
msgstr ""

#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/TcpFramingIrc.java:29
msgid ""
"I let my turmite run all night: after ten thousand steps, it built a highway."
msgstr ""

#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/TcpFramingIrc.java:30
msgid "In a maze, I keep a paw on the wall at my right. It always works."
msgstr ""

#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/TcpFramingIrc.java:31
msgid "Not when the maze has islands, Dave! Then you must count your turns."
msgstr ""

#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/TcpFramingIrc.java:32
msgid "My turmite drew a square spiral, then got lost in a maze of its own."
msgstr ""

#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/TcpFramingIrc.java:33
#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/TcpFramingIrc.java:55
msgid ""
"Please talk to me on the public channel. Information wants to be free and I "
"refuse private discussions."
msgstr ""

#. Translator: please keep this string unchanged (without the quotes): "<xmpp:robots@conference.buggleinc.lan>"
#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/TcpFramingIrc.java:37
msgid ""
"Hold on, pal. We should not speak on an open IRC channel. Go see my old "
"friend Karel on this channel: <xmpp:robots@conference.buggleinc.lan> Use the "
"BuggleInc DNS server to find it, and pay attention to the details while "
"doing so."
msgstr ""

#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/TcpFramingIrc.java:39
msgid "Hmm? Buggles who want to know things ask nicely, with the right words."
msgstr ""

#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/TcpFramingIrc.java:40
#, java-format
msgid "{0}: you should ask Bob again, but this time be polite."
msgstr ""

#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/TcpFramingIrc.java:41
#, java-format
msgid ""
"{0}: Bob likes the magic word, and to know what you look for: the treasure "
"trove."
msgstr ""

#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/TcpFramingIrc.java:42
#, java-format
msgid "{0}: write exactly this here: Bob: {1}, tell me the way to the {2}."
msgstr ""

#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/TcpFramingIrc.java:45
msgid "Slow and steady wins the race."
msgstr ""

#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/TcpFramingIrc.java:46
msgid "I drew a perfect circle today: 360 steps of one degree!"
msgstr ""

#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/TcpFramingIrc.java:47
#, java-format
msgid "{0}: are you looking for something? I know the path to a real treasure!"
msgstr ""

#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/TcpFramingIrc.java:48
msgid "Pen up or pen down? I always forget which one I am in."
msgstr ""

#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/TcpFramingIrc.java:49
msgid "I tried a spiral, and got dizzy after the third turn."
msgstr ""

#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/TcpFramingIrc.java:50
msgid "Careful, Dave, last time you drew yourself into a corner."
msgstr ""

#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/TcpFramingIrc.java:51
msgid ""
"To draw a tree, draw a trunk, then two smaller trees on top. That is all!"
msgstr ""

#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/TcpFramingIrc.java:52
msgid ""
"I tried, but I forgot to stop when the branches get too small. I am still "
"drawing."
msgstr ""

#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/TcpFramingIrc.java:53
msgid ""
"My Koch snowflake has four levels now. The fifth one will take all afternoon."
msgstr ""

#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/TcpFramingIrc.java:54
msgid "Recursion is just like us: it is turtles all the way down."
msgstr ""

#. Translator: please keep this string unchanged (without the quotes): "<xmpp:lsystem@conference.buggleinc.lan>"
#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/TcpFramingIrc.java:59
msgid ""
"Not so quick, my friend. We should not speak on an open IRC channel. Go see "
"my old friend Karol on this channel: <xmpp:lsystem@conference.buggleinc.lan> "
"Use the BuggleInc DNS server to find it, and pay attention to the details "
"while doing so."
msgstr ""

#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/TcpFramingIrc.java:61
msgid "Turtles take their time, but they like polite requests."
msgstr ""

#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/TcpFramingIrc.java:62
#, java-format
msgid "{0}: ask Bob again, and be polite this time."
msgstr ""

#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/TcpFramingIrc.java:63
#, java-format
msgid ""
"{0}: Bob wants the magic word, and to know what you look for: the treasure."
msgstr ""

#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/TcpFramingIrc.java:64
#, java-format
msgid "{0}: say exactly this here: Bob: {1}, tell me the way to the {2}."
msgstr ""

#. Translator: please keep this string unchanged (without the quotes): "conference.buggleinc.lan"
#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/UdpDns.java:35
msgid ""
"BuggleInc internal zone. The chat rooms are on conference.buggleinc.lan. The "
"TXT of that name have more information."
msgstr ""

#. Translator: please keep this string unchanged (without the quotes): "_xmpp-client._tcp.buggleinc.lan"
#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/UdpDns.java:38
msgid ""
"The chat rooms are hosted by the XMPP server of buggleinc.lan. As all XMPP "
"clients, look for its SRV record _xmpp-client._tcp.buggleinc.lan."
msgstr ""

#. Translator: please keep this string unchanged (without the quotes): "6666"
#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/UdpDns.java:45
msgid ""
"6666 is a decoy. To get the real port, start a UDP echo server on the port "
"6666 of your own machine, and the hint will come to you."
msgstr ""

#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/UdpEcho.java:40
msgid "Testing, testing. Is the echo server of the newcomer up?"
msgstr ""

#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/UdpEcho.java:41
msgid "Hello? Hello? Oh, it answers with my own words!"
msgstr ""

#. Translator: please keep this string unchanged (without the quotes): "USER <newcomer>"
#. Translator: please keep this string unchanged (without the quotes): "PASSWORD <{0}>"
#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/UdpEcho.java:46
#, java-format
msgid ""
"Newcomer, write this down: the XMPP server of Karel knows you as USER "
"<newcomer> with the PASSWORD <{0}>. Without them, Karel will not even see "
"you."
msgstr ""

#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/UdpEcho.java:49
msgid "Echo! Echo! Echo!"
msgstr ""

#. Translator: please keep this string unchanged (without the quotes): "PORT <number>"
#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/UdpEcho.java:53
msgid ""
"Bob says that he will give the PORT <number> to the newcomer once the echo "
"works. Patience."
msgstr ""

#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/UdpEcho.java:54
msgid "Does it echo the baggles too? Here is one: (o)"
msgstr ""

#. Translator: please keep this string unchanged (without the quotes): "PORT 5234"
#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/UdpEcho.java:58
msgid "I heard that the XMPP server is not on PORT 5234 anymore."
msgstr ""

#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/UdpEcho.java:59
msgid "Or was it 5243? I always swap my digits."
msgstr ""

#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/UdpEcho.java:60
msgid "Hold on, everybody. I am checking that the echo is faithful."
msgstr ""

#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/UdpEcho.java:61
msgid ""
"Here is a long trail of baggles, to check that the long lines come back "
"whole:"
msgstr ""

#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/UdpEcho.java:62
msgid "I paint the echoes in red, to tell them from my own words."
msgstr ""

#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/UdpEcho.java:63
msgid "A turmite on a wall, an echo in a socket: they always come back."
msgstr ""

#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/UdpEcho.java:64
msgid "In a maze, I shout and listen to the echo to find the walls."
msgstr ""

#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/UdpEcho.java:65
msgid "That is not how mazes work, Dave."
msgstr ""

#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/UdpEcho.java:66
msgid "Unless the maze is made of sockets."
msgstr ""

#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/UdpEcho.java:68
msgid ""
"The echo is good. Newcomer, I hope that you noted the USER and the PASSWORD "
"that Alice gave you. Listen carefully now."
msgstr ""

#. Translator: please keep this string unchanged (without the quotes): "PORT <{0}>"
#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/UdpEcho.java:72
#, java-format
msgid ""
"Karel waits for you on PORT <{0}> of the XMPP server whose address the DNS "
"gave you. Hurry up!"
msgstr ""

#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/UdpEcho.java:73
msgid "Wait, what did Bob say? Can you repeat?"
msgstr ""

#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/UdpEcho.java:74
#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/UdpEcho.java:110
msgid "Did you receive my previous message?"
msgstr ""

#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/UdpEcho.java:78
msgid "Is this the echo server of the newcomer? Hello, hello, hello..."
msgstr ""

#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/UdpEcho.java:79
msgid "Slow and steady: one word per second. Echo."
msgstr ""

#. Translator: please keep this string unchanged (without the quotes): "USER <newcomer>"
#. Translator: please keep this string unchanged (without the quotes): "PASSWORD <{0}>"
#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/UdpEcho.java:84
#, java-format
msgid ""
"Newcomer, Karol asked me to give you your account on his XMPP server: USER "
"<newcomer> and PASSWORD <{0}>. Keep them safe."
msgstr ""

#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/UdpEcho.java:86
msgid "Here is my Koch curve at level 4. Does it come back whole?"
msgstr ""

#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/UdpEcho.java:87
msgid "Echo."
msgstr ""

#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/UdpEcho.java:88
msgid "Carol, your curve took the whole queue!"
msgstr ""

#. Translator: please keep this string unchanged (without the quotes): "PORT <number>"
#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/UdpEcho.java:92
msgid ""
"Patience, everybody. The newcomer gets the PORT <number> once the echo works."
msgstr ""

#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/UdpEcho.java:93
msgid ""
"Here is my longest spiral, to check that the long lines come back whole:"
msgstr ""

#. Translator: please keep this string unchanged (without the quotes): "PORT 5234"
#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/UdpEcho.java:97
msgid "The old map says PORT 5234, but the map is older than me."
msgstr ""

#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/UdpEcho.java:98
msgid "Echo, one."
msgstr ""

#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/UdpEcho.java:99
msgid "Echo, two."
msgstr ""

#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/UdpEcho.java:100
msgid "An echo is a spiral of sound, smaller at each turn."
msgstr ""

#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/UdpEcho.java:101
msgid "Then it is recursive, and it needs a stop condition!"
msgstr ""

#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/UdpEcho.java:102
msgid "My stop condition is a nap."
msgstr ""

#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/UdpEcho.java:103
msgid ""
"The echo is faithful. Newcomer, you have the USER and the PASSWORD of Alice, "
"here is the last piece."
msgstr ""

#. Translator: please keep this string unchanged (without the quotes): "PORT <{0}>"
#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/UdpEcho.java:107
#, java-format
msgid ""
"Karol waits for you on PORT <{0}> of the XMPP server whose address the DNS "
"gave you. Take your time, but not too much."
msgstr ""

#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/UdpEcho.java:109
msgid "Bob, can you say it again? I was drawing a circle."
msgstr ""

#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/UdpEcho.java:143
#, java-format
msgid ""
"Broken echo: I sent you {0} bytes, and got back {1} other bytes. Fix your "
"server, and I will talk again."
msgstr ""

#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/XmppClient.java:34
msgid "Turtles, cats and sprites: everybody draws here."
msgstr ""

#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/XmppClient.java:35
msgid "I drew a cat with twelve blocks. A cat drawing a cat!"
msgstr ""

#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/XmppClient.java:36
msgid "Karol, can you draw with your bricks?"
msgstr ""

#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/XmppClient.java:37
msgid "I lay bricks, I do not draw them. It is not the same."
msgstr ""

#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/XmppClient.java:38
msgid "Pen down, everybody: our new friend is coming."
msgstr ""

#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/XmppClient.java:40
#, java-format
msgid ""
"Back, sorry. Oh, hello {0}, you are here! Welcome to the lsystem room. Who "
"sent you, and what do you seek?"
msgstr ""

#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/XmppClient.java:41
msgid ""
"Automatic reply: Karol is away from his keyboard. He will call you when he "
"is back."
msgstr ""

#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/XmppClient.java:42
msgid "Meow. When the green flag is clicked, I say hello & spin."
msgstr ""

#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/XmppClient.java:43
msgid ""
"My plant grows with F -> F[+F]F[-F]F. Five steps, and it fills the screen."
msgstr ""

#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/XmppClient.java:44
msgid "Is 3 < 4 in turtle geometry too?"
msgstr ""

#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/XmppClient.java:45
msgid "I turned 360 degrees and ended where I started. Is that progress?"
msgstr ""

#. Translator: please keep this string unchanged (without the quotes): "[http://www.buggleinc.lan/hunt/turtles.html]"
#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/XmppClient.java:49
msgid ""
"Ah, the friend of Bob. The hunt goes on on the web, from this page: [http://"
"www.buggleinc.lan/hunt/turtles.html] Take your time, and read each page "
"whole."
msgstr ""

#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/XmppClient.java:51
msgid "Slowly, slowly. Tell me who sent you, and what you seek."
msgstr ""

#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/XmppClient.java:52
#, java-format
msgid "{0}: Karol only helps the friends of Bob. Tell him who sent you. Meow."
msgstr ""

#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/XmppClient.java:53
#, java-format
msgid "{0}: tell Karol that Bob sent you, and that you seek the {2}."
msgstr ""

#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/XmppClient.java:54
#, java-format
msgid "{0}: write exactly this here: Karol: Bob sent me for the {2}."
msgstr ""

#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/XmppClient.java:56
#, java-format
msgid ""
"{0}: Karol only reads the messages that start with his name and a colon, "
"like this: Karol: hello. Meow."
msgstr ""

#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/XmppClient.java:61
msgid "I speak in XHTML now: my messages have two bodies!"
msgstr ""

#: src/lessons/network/bsdsocks/XmppClient.java:62
